  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDEA: Democracy, gender and youth</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IDEA: Demokrati, j&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhet och ungdomar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the intervention was to contribute to the strengthening of the Bolivian democracy by promoting an integral participation of the youth and women in political parties while also providing technical assistance to the National Electoral Body. The five target regions under this initiative were La Paz, Santa Cruz, Cochabamba, Tarija and Beni.
The four components of the contribution, as developed and implemented by IDEA International, in the 5 mentioned Bolivian regions, were: i) the strengthening of some municipal/regional management issues, ii) the consolidation of a deeper gender equality participation, iii) the promotion of a more&#xA0;active and deep political participation of the youth, and iv) the improvement of the quality of electoral services delivered by the Bolivian Electoral Body.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det projekt som f&#xF6;resl&#xE5;s av IDEA International syftar till att bidra till att st&#xE4;rka den bolivianska demokratin och ut&#xF6;vandet av medborgarnas r&#xE4;ttigheter genom att fr&#xE4;mja deltagandet av ungdoms- och kvinnorganisationer, samt samordningen med de politiska partierna, de autonoma regionala regeringerna (GAD) och den nationella valmyndigheten. Insatsen genomf&#xF6;rs utifr&#xE5;n fyra huvudlinjer med syfte att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra:  i) offentlig f&#xF6;rvaltning, ii) kvinnornas politiska deltagande, iii) ungdomspolitiska deltagande, och iv) valmyndighetens institutionella kapacitet. Det anses vara en forts&#xE4;ttning p&#xE5; bidraget 55180029 (Kvinnors ledarskap och medborgarnas deltagande p&#xE5; lokal niv&#xE5; - IDEA)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project proposed by IDEA International seeks to contribute to the strengthening of the  Bolivian democracy and to the full exercise of citizen rights, by promoting a coordinated participation between youth and women&apos;s organizations, the political parties, the autonomous departmental governments (GAD) and the National Electoral Body. The four strategic lines of action that will guide IDEA&apos;s initiative to achieve its objectives are aimed to enhance: i)public management, ii) the women&apos;s political participation, iii) the youth&apos;s political participation, and iv) the institutional capacity of the electoral body. It is considered to be a continuation of contribution 55180029 (Women Leadership and Citizen Participation at the local level - IDEA)</narrative>
  </description>
